7
00:00:32,600 --> 00:00:33,920
I really do like you.

8
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,360
Oh, Soh.

9
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:04,640
I'm sorry.

10
00:01:05,960 --> 00:01:07,440
My intrusive thoughts just won.

11
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:09,360
I'm such a jerk.

12
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,280
I was totally taking advantage
of the moment.

13
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,400
Do you...

14
00:01:12,960 --> 00:01:14,560
really like me, P'Three?

15
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:26,480
If you're still not sure,

16
00:01:27,440 --> 00:01:29,200
you don't have to like me back yet.

17
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:32,280
But can I ask you one thing?

18
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,840
Please don't run away from me again.

19
00:01:38,640 --> 00:01:40,040
Don't run away from my feelings

20
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:42,080
that I have only for you.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:50,920
Or...

22
00:01:51,600 --> 00:01:54,120
have you not forgiven me
for what just happened?

23
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:56,080
Soh, I'm sorry. I mean...

24
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:58,720
You can scold me or even punch me.

25
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:00,600
I'll take whatever you throw at me.

26
00:02:02,760 --> 00:02:03,560
P'Three...

27
00:02:06,400 --> 00:02:07,880
Please open your eyes.

28
00:02:10,560 --> 00:02:12,400
I'm not going to punch you,

29
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:15,560
and I never thought
about running away, either.

30
00:02:25,760 --> 00:02:27,560
Since you didn't say anything,

31
00:02:27,960 --> 00:02:29,520
my heart literally sank.

32
00:02:31,760 --> 00:02:34,080
To be honest,
I'm feeling pretty awkward, too.

33
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:36,720
You suddenly told me you like me.

34
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:40,920
Then...

35
00:02:42,720 --> 00:02:45,440
shall we take things one step at a time?

36
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,280
You can take your time to think.

37
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:50,600
You don't have to
give me an answer right away.

38
00:02:58,480 --> 00:02:59,720
Let's play a game instead.

39
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,880
What kind of game?

40
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,400
The game of winning Derpy Kid's heart.

41
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,840
I'll make everything clear.

42
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:17,240
You can try
the one-week free trial first

43
00:03:17,800 --> 00:03:18,920
before giving me your answer.

44
00:03:22,040 --> 00:03:23,080
If you're down,

45
00:03:25,560 --> 00:03:27,000
the start button is right here.

46
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,080
I'm just kidding.

47
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:39,360
You don't have to press it just yet.

48
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:45,520
Keep it as my reward
for when I win this game.

49
00:03:56,280 --> 00:04:01,040
♪Birthday but with me♪

50
00:04:01,080 --> 00:04:04,360
♪Every time, it's just me and me only♪

51
00:04:04,400 --> 00:04:08,040
♪What's this feeling? I've got no clue,♪

52
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:10,080
♪Could it be I'm missing you?♪

53
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:11,480
♪(Am I missing you?)♪

54
00:04:11,520 --> 00:04:16,280
♪Birthday but with me♪

55
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:19,400
♪Why is it always happening to me?♪

56
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:23,160
♪The more it happens, the more I see♪

57
00:04:23,800 --> 00:04:26,040
♪Yeah, it must be♪

58
00:04:40,520 --> 00:04:42,880
You can try
the one-week free trial first.

59
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:46,920
If you're down,

60
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,920
the start button is right here.

61
00:05:25,560 --> 00:05:27,320
P'Three, help me!

62
00:05:27,400 --> 00:05:28,680
Help me, please.

63
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,800
Your knight in shining armor
is on his way.

64
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:39,760
What?

65
00:05:40,160 --> 00:05:42,240
Where the hell are you going?
I'm dead.

66
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:43,080
Well...

67
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:51,760
Whoa,

68
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,960
excuse me, Son of Wanphen.

69
00:05:54,320 --> 00:05:56,320
My Carry had one bar of HP left,

70
00:05:56,440 --> 00:05:58,120
but you were busy
helping the full-HP Support?

71
00:05:58,240 --> 00:06:01,080
Are you here to play for B.S. Brothers
or just Soh, huh?

72
00:06:02,640 --> 00:06:03,920
You guys need to stop whining.

73
00:06:04,120 --> 00:06:06,200
I'll treat you to mookrata, okay?

74
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:09,840
You threw the game so hard
you owe me a salmon buffet.

75
00:06:10,240 --> 00:06:12,880
Whoa, you're getting real sneaky.

76
00:06:13,240 --> 00:06:14,920
You're getting good
at taking advantage of the chaos.

77
00:06:15,880 --> 00:06:18,560
Hey, our team won three games already.

78
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:20,840
We've got the momentum now.

79
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:23,000
- So...
- We've gotta keep pushing!

80
00:06:23,040 --> 00:06:24,120
I think we should take a break.

81
00:06:24,640 --> 00:06:25,520
- What?
- What?

82
00:06:27,200 --> 00:06:29,360
Look, let me tell you something.

83
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:33,400
Our team's HP
is running pretty low right now.

84
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:34,600
We're in terrible form,

85
00:06:34,680 --> 00:06:37,240
and the tournament
has been dragging on for so long.

86
00:06:37,680 --> 00:06:39,360
I think you guys should rest,

87
00:06:39,720 --> 00:06:40,880
and while you're resting,

88
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,800
don't let your HP drop
as low as it did in the game, got it?

89
00:06:47,480 --> 00:06:48,840
From the look of it,

90
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:51,800
he just wants to go
on a honeymoon with P'Jane.

91
00:06:53,000 --> 00:06:54,400
You've got a big mouth, Laem,

92
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:56,160
acting like you're...

93
00:06:56,360 --> 00:06:58,000
living under my bed or something.

94
00:06:58,680 --> 00:07:00,920
Fine. Since that's
the attitude you want to take,

95
00:07:01,120 --> 00:07:02,840
forget the break. Keep practicing.

96
00:07:02,880 --> 00:07:05,640
- What? No! We need a break.
- Whoa, chill. Please give us a break.

97
00:07:06,640 --> 00:07:07,680
You and your big mouth.

98
00:07:07,960 --> 00:07:10,320
Anyway, I'll see you guys next week.

99
00:07:13,360 --> 00:07:15,200
See you then, P'Three.

100
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:16,760
Hey, wait a sec, Soh.

101
00:07:18,920 --> 00:07:20,840
I found this really cute game.

102
00:07:20,960 --> 00:07:21,640
You should give it a try.

103
00:07:23,760 --> 00:07:27,280
Is it an FPS? What kind of game is it?

104
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:29,320
Kind...

105
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:30,960
of normal.

106
00:07:31,840 --> 00:07:34,000
No download needed.
I'll send you the link.

107
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:37,560
Does it have to be right now?

108
00:07:40,400 --> 00:07:43,240
Not right now, but you have to play it.

109
00:07:43,560 --> 00:07:46,360
Don't bail on me,
or I'll be really upset.

110
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:48,080
Okay.

111
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,000
I'll give it a try.

112
00:07:50,360 --> 00:07:51,680
You promised.

113
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:54,000
I'm off, then.

114
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,160
Make sure to play it.

115
00:07:57,640 --> 00:07:58,240
Catch you later.

116
00:08:06,520 --> 00:08:08,720
(Winning Derpy Kid's Heart)

117
00:08:14,600 --> 00:08:15,760
(Someone wants to
spend their day off with you.)

118
00:08:15,800 --> 00:08:18,080
(Will you give them a chance
to go on a date?)

119
00:08:19,200 --> 00:08:20,560
What are you doing, P'Three?

120
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,440
Hello, ma boy.

121
00:08:39,560 --> 00:08:40,680
Stunned, aren't you?

122
00:08:41,920 --> 00:08:43,600
I know I'm incredibly handsome,

123
00:08:43,920 --> 00:08:45,920
and I know I'm looking super hot today.

124
00:08:48,800 --> 00:08:49,480
You do look handsome,

125
00:08:49,480 --> 00:08:52,240
but whose car is this?

126
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,320
Get in. Come on.

127
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:11,120
(Three hours ago)

128
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:17,880
Yes!

129
00:09:25,680 --> 00:09:26,440
What should we do?

130
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,240
Watch a movie?

131
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:28,680
What should we watch? What's out now?

132
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:29,160
Hold on.

133
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:30,720
A meal?

134
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,440
My dearest brother, Four.

135
00:09:41,480 --> 00:09:43,680
Your favorite brother
needs a little favor.

136
00:09:46,800 --> 00:09:48,720
Hey there, little brother.

137
00:09:48,880 --> 00:09:51,080
Wow, I missed you so much.
Come here!

138
00:09:54,680 --> 00:09:57,760
- There, there. Let's hug. I missed you.
- Don't touch me.

139
00:09:57,760 --> 00:09:58,800
- Go away.
- What?

140
00:09:59,040 --> 00:10:01,400
Stop faking it.
As if you ever wanted to hug me.

141
00:10:01,760 --> 00:10:02,880
Don't expose me like that.

142
00:10:06,520 --> 00:10:07,240
The key.

143
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:08,960
- What?
- Give me the key.

144
00:10:10,480 --> 00:10:11,160
Here.

145
00:10:13,520 --> 00:10:15,280
Dad's been wanting you
to come pick it up forever.

146
00:10:15,480 --> 00:10:16,200
It's just cluttering the place.

147
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:17,080
Cluttering?

148
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:20,040
Fine, I'll keep it, then.

149
00:10:21,160 --> 00:10:22,400
You little brat, come here!

150
00:10:22,480 --> 00:10:24,040
Jeez, leave me alone.

151
00:10:24,080 --> 00:10:25,440
Where did you get these looks from?

152
00:10:25,480 --> 00:10:26,880
- Me, obviously. Come here.
- Go away.

153
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,720
Let me go. I've got plans for dinner.

154
00:10:28,920 --> 00:10:30,520
- Dinner?
- Yeah.

155
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:31,640
Are you dating someone?

156
00:10:32,040 --> 00:10:33,800
Show me their Insta. Let me see it.

157
00:10:33,880 --> 00:10:34,320
Mind your own business.

158
00:10:35,040 --> 00:10:36,920
As if you ever cared.

159
00:10:37,720 --> 00:10:38,480
Are you mad at me?

160
00:10:39,720 --> 00:10:41,200
You wish.

161
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:43,560
Fine.

162
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,760
Anyway, if you ever have any problems,

163
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:47,960
you can always
tell your big brother, kid.

164
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,480
Maybe worry about yourself first.

165
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:53,880
I'm doing just fine.

166
00:10:55,080 --> 00:10:55,960
Bye.

167
00:10:56,480 --> 00:10:57,960
Wait, want a ride?

168
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,200
- No, I already called one.
- Oh, you don't want a ride from me?

169
00:11:00,240 --> 00:11:02,400
- Nah.
- Okay, then. See ya.

170
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:05,800
Ouch!

171
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:14,800
Where are we going, P'Three?

172
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:18,440
I'll keep it under wraps for now.

173
00:11:19,160 --> 00:11:20,080
I want it to be a surprise.

174
00:11:23,800 --> 00:11:26,440
I kinda thought
you wouldn't agree to come.

175
00:11:27,880 --> 00:11:30,840
Do you have any idea
how long it took me to code that game?

176
00:11:30,840 --> 00:11:32,120
I barely got any sleep.

177
00:11:33,480 --> 00:11:34,760
Was the coding the hard part?

178
00:11:34,800 --> 00:11:36,720
It was choosing
my best-looking photo. Hey!

179
00:11:38,240 --> 00:11:40,040
You really jumped there just now.

180
00:11:41,080 --> 00:11:42,160
P'Three, watch out!

181
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,400
Roger that.

182
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:45,560
You don't have to worry

183
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,360
because ever since I started driving,

184
00:11:47,560 --> 00:11:50,280
I've never had a single accident.

185
00:11:51,760 --> 00:11:52,960
- Watch out!
- Whoa!

186
00:11:55,280 --> 00:11:57,160
Are you even driving?

187
00:11:57,200 --> 00:11:58,880
Where are you going, the moon?

188
00:12:02,280 --> 00:12:04,800
Soh, are you okay?
Are you hurt anywhere?

189
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:06,800
Did you hit your head?
Are you in any pain?

190
00:12:06,880 --> 00:12:09,120
I'm so sorry.
I should've been more careful.

191
00:12:09,160 --> 00:12:10,960
- It's my fault that...
- I'm fine.

192
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:12,680
I'm okay.

193
00:12:13,640 --> 00:12:14,280
Are you sure?

194
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:16,600
If anything hurts,

195
00:12:17,040 --> 00:12:18,280
you need to tell me.

196
00:12:19,360 --> 00:12:20,120
I'm seriously okay.

197
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:23,040
A little damage like this
is nothing to a Support like me.

198
00:12:25,680 --> 00:12:26,920
Let's get going.

199
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:30,160
I'm dying to know
where you're taking me.

200
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,280
You're sure you're not hurt anywhere?

201
00:12:34,680 --> 00:12:35,480
I'm not hurt.

202
00:12:49,120 --> 00:12:49,880
Please have a seat.

203
00:13:00,520 --> 00:13:01,440
Here's the menu, sir.

204
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:10,160
You can order whatever you want.

205
00:13:12,440 --> 00:13:15,560
Do you have any recommendations?

206
00:13:23,120 --> 00:13:24,120
How about...

207
00:13:25,160 --> 00:13:27,040
Escargot Louboutin?

208
00:13:31,560 --> 00:13:32,640
I'll have this one.

209
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:33,840
Certainly.

210
00:13:37,920 --> 00:13:38,640
Thank you.

211
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:41,600
Do you come here often?

212
00:13:42,840 --> 00:13:43,840
It's my regular spot.

213
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:45,760
Usually, it's incredibly hard
to get a reservation here.

214
00:13:46,080 --> 00:13:47,200
But for you,

215
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:48,480
it was a breeze.

216
00:13:58,560 --> 00:14:00,960
I always order this dish
when I come here.

217
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:06,280
Is this your go-to meal?

218
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:09,640
It is.

219
00:14:21,040 --> 00:14:22,480
This is my absolute favorite,

220
00:14:22,480 --> 00:14:24,640
Escargot Louboutin...

221
00:14:32,240 --> 00:14:34,120
You make it look so delicious.

222
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:35,720
Here.

223
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:42,120
I think I'll just go
with a salad instead.

224
00:14:42,560 --> 00:14:44,200
One salad, please.

225
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,800
You're not having the Louboutin?

226
00:14:55,040 --> 00:14:57,240
(Thought you said you'd tell me
about your old friend.)

227
00:15:03,920 --> 00:15:05,040
(Man, you're so nosy.)

228
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:09,040
(If you're this curious, come to me
and I'll tell you.)

229
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:12,280
(Fine by me. We'll finally meet.)

230
00:15:16,120 --> 00:15:17,160
(Where at?)

231
00:15:18,800 --> 00:15:20,280
(How about Bananax2?)

232
00:15:23,800 --> 00:15:26,160
(Then hurry up. Last one there pays.)

233
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,760
Actually, this place
offers a special performance, too.

234
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,600
I'm sure you're going to love it.

235
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:44,760
Really?

236
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:07,680
Cheers.

237
00:16:08,480 --> 00:16:09,120
Okay.

238
00:16:30,480 --> 00:16:31,040
Sh...

239
00:16:34,280 --> 00:16:35,720
Sh*t.

240
00:16:40,880 --> 00:16:43,600
We're really sorry, sir.

241
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:58,960
Good thing they're okay.

242
00:17:00,600 --> 00:17:01,640
As cute as ever.

243
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:08,600
We're really sorry, sir.

244
00:17:08,920 --> 00:17:11,280
We're going to bring you a new cake.

245
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,840
It's fine. I'm cutting back
on sugar anyway.

246
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:15,240
This is already sweet enough.

247
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:34,840
Please.

248
00:17:41,680 --> 00:17:42,440
Do you like it?

249
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:48,920
Uh, I mean...

250
00:17:49,320 --> 00:17:51,000
do you like our first date?

251
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:53,240
Well, aside from the mishap,

252
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:55,480
the food and the vibe
were pretty good.

253
00:17:57,520 --> 00:17:58,200
Well,

254
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:00,480
I like it.

255
00:18:04,640 --> 00:18:05,920
Being this close,

256
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:07,840
it's easy to tell what you're thinking.

257
00:18:11,480 --> 00:18:15,040
I don't think I'm cut out
for dates like this.

258
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:18,280
I'm feeling a bit nervous.

259
00:18:18,280 --> 00:18:19,040
Right?

260
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:21,360
I've been trying so hard to act cool.

261
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,360
You're not the only one.
I'm nervous, too.

262
00:18:24,680 --> 00:18:26,840
This is my first time
eating at a place like this, too.

263
00:18:27,680 --> 00:18:29,600
I usually just go for mala hotpot.

264
00:18:32,360 --> 00:18:34,440
I don't want our first date
to end in disappointment.

265
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,560
Can I restart
the game of winning your heart?

266
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:40,200
(Winning Derpy Kid's Heart)

267
00:18:43,160 --> 00:18:44,800
Then from now on,

268
00:18:45,400 --> 00:18:47,720
don't take me
to do anything too fancy.

269
00:18:49,200 --> 00:18:51,000
It was so fancy I got all nervous.

270
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:54,000
I promise.

271
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:57,280
No more escargot snails
or orchestras or whatever.

272
00:19:05,040 --> 00:19:05,760
Let's go.

273
00:19:20,960 --> 00:19:23,560
How did you know I wanted to come here?

274
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:26,360
Well, you see,

275
00:19:26,560 --> 00:19:29,680
I happened to see someone
liking a video about capybaras.

276
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:33,320
Wow, I'm so attentive,

277
00:19:34,240 --> 00:19:34,880
aren't I?

278
00:19:40,040 --> 00:19:43,040
By the way, why did you want
to come to the zoo?

279
00:19:43,280 --> 00:19:44,080
Do you like animals?

280
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:46,160
Yes, I do.

281
00:19:48,040 --> 00:19:51,120
Good thing my friends
call me an animal, too. Do you like me?

282
00:19:52,480 --> 00:19:53,360
What did you say?

283
00:19:53,920 --> 00:19:56,640
Oh, sorry.
It was just an intrusive thought.

284
00:19:57,040 --> 00:19:58,760
Do you come here often?

285
00:20:00,560 --> 00:20:02,640
I used to come here a lot
with my parents,

286
00:20:03,280 --> 00:20:07,640
but I haven't been back
since my dad passed away.

287
00:20:09,440 --> 00:20:11,200
It's nice being at the zoo today.

288
00:20:12,120 --> 00:20:13,320
Feels like going back in time.

289
00:20:14,120 --> 00:20:15,880
Then let's be kids again.

290
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:18,440
I'll do everything
just like your dad used to,

291
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:22,000
though I probably
won't be as good as him.

292
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:26,320
Anyway, whatever you wanna do
or wherever you wanna go,

293
00:20:26,360 --> 00:20:28,440
just let me know. I'll make it happen.

294
00:20:49,720 --> 00:20:53,000
Mom, look.
He even has a bodyguard. So cool.

295
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,600
Don't point at him. Sorry.

296
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:04,360
Would you like something cold
to drink, Young Master?

297
00:21:14,680 --> 00:21:16,560
Shall we go
find something cold to drink?

298
00:21:18,200 --> 00:21:18,800
Let's go.

299
00:21:19,280 --> 00:21:20,200
Alright.

300
00:21:30,480 --> 00:21:31,480
Look, P'Three!

301
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:33,360
Hey, what do you mean? I'm right here.

302
00:21:33,560 --> 00:21:35,360
No, I was just pointing.

303
00:21:36,720 --> 00:21:38,880
Believe it or not, I never came
to the zoo when I was a kid.

304
00:21:40,600 --> 00:21:41,480
No way.

305
00:21:41,560 --> 00:21:42,240
I'm serious.

306
00:21:42,280 --> 00:21:43,720
Are you pulling my leg?

307
00:21:45,200 --> 00:21:47,880
When I was little, my parents always
made me watch the gold shop,

308
00:21:48,520 --> 00:21:49,520
so I never got to go out.

309
00:21:53,080 --> 00:21:55,200
That's why I grew up being a homebody.

310
00:21:57,600 --> 00:21:59,240
Actually, a gamer.

311
00:21:59,720 --> 00:22:00,720
Just like you.

312
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:03,400
You've got it all over your mouth.

313
00:22:08,040 --> 00:22:08,840
P'Three,

314
00:22:09,720 --> 00:22:10,560
that's WuKong.

315
00:22:11,000 --> 00:22:11,920
- What skin...
- Mini WuKong.

316
00:22:11,960 --> 00:22:12,800
Mini WuKong?

317
00:22:12,800 --> 00:22:13,720
What skin is this?

318
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:15,600
Everyone who plays WuKong
is handsome, though.

319
00:22:15,640 --> 00:22:17,360
Hey, are you complimenting yourself?

320
00:22:17,640 --> 00:22:18,640
Oh, you can tell?

321
00:22:22,440 --> 00:22:23,640
Believe it or not,

322
00:22:23,880 --> 00:22:26,040
I used to travel quite a lot back then.

323
00:22:26,520 --> 00:22:29,200
I wasn't the homebody nerd
you think I was.

324
00:22:30,040 --> 00:22:30,920
That's nice.

325
00:22:31,160 --> 00:22:32,520
So you traveled with your family?

326
00:22:33,440 --> 00:22:36,360
Yes, my dad loved
taking me to other provinces.

327
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:38,480
I've been everywhere.
North, south, east, and west.

328
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:44,440
My dad used to say I was very cute

329
00:22:44,480 --> 00:22:45,680
with my chubby cheeks.

330
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:49,000
So he took a ton of photos of me

331
00:22:49,080 --> 00:22:52,120
'cause he knew I wouldn't be as cute
once I grew up.

332
00:22:53,400 --> 00:22:55,400
If your dad ever came to me in a dream,

333
00:22:55,440 --> 00:22:56,640
I'd tell him myself

334
00:22:57,200 --> 00:23:00,160
that you're still just as cute
now that you're grown up.

335
00:23:00,480 --> 00:23:02,320
Since you've grown up this much,

336
00:23:02,320 --> 00:23:04,000
can I take a photo of you now?

337
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:06,440
- Sure.
- Great, come here.

338
00:23:07,240 --> 00:23:09,440
- Come on. Oh, look. He's right here.
- Whoa.

339
00:23:21,400 --> 00:23:24,040
Right. How am I supposed to see them?

340
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:28,720
Hey, P'Three!

341
00:23:28,960 --> 00:23:30,520
What are you doing?

342
00:23:36,120 --> 00:23:37,360
Did you see the sloth yet?

343
00:23:37,600 --> 00:23:40,040
- Yeah, he's huge.
- Want another look?

344
00:23:40,360 --> 00:23:41,920
One, two, three.

345
00:23:50,360 --> 00:23:52,080
- You actually look like them.
- You, too.

346
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:53,360
- I don't.
- You do.

347
00:23:53,400 --> 00:23:54,760
- No, I don't.
- Check the photo.

348
00:24:00,080 --> 00:24:01,040
Cute.

349
00:24:05,520 --> 00:24:07,720
So, what's your type?

350
00:24:08,680 --> 00:24:09,480
Do you have a type?

351
00:24:11,440 --> 00:24:14,000
I haven't really thought about that yet.

352
00:24:18,280 --> 00:24:19,960
Hey, no worries.

353
00:24:20,560 --> 00:24:21,840
I don't have a type, either.

354
00:24:22,440 --> 00:24:26,800
As long as I'm comfortable
being around them, that's enough.

355
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:30,280
You're answering like a celebrity.

356
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:33,040
Hey, I'm a famous streamer, you know.

357
00:24:36,840 --> 00:24:38,440
Whoa, P'Three!

358
00:24:38,720 --> 00:24:40,000
Look at its face.

359
00:24:41,200 --> 00:24:42,760
It's just like the video I saw.

360
00:24:44,760 --> 00:24:46,080
The ears are twitching.

361
00:24:48,200 --> 00:24:49,560
Shall we take a selfie?

362
00:24:50,560 --> 00:24:51,320
Of course.

363
00:24:54,800 --> 00:24:56,000
Excuse me.

364
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:59,840
Are you P'Three from B.S. Brothers?

365
00:24:59,880 --> 00:25:00,680
Yes, I am.

366
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,840
Can I take a photo with you?

367
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:07,040
Sure, come on.

368
00:25:07,760 --> 00:25:11,400
Guys, come on. He said yes!

369
00:25:11,720 --> 00:25:13,760
- Yay!
- Yay!

370
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:15,480
Wait...

371
00:25:15,960 --> 00:25:17,240
Look, Doraemon!

372
00:25:18,120 --> 00:25:20,280
- Oh, P'Three...
- Hey, P'Three!

373
00:25:20,280 --> 00:25:21,240
Hey!

374
00:25:21,720 --> 00:25:22,680
Wait!

375
00:25:27,680 --> 00:25:29,040
- P'Three!
- P'Three!

376
00:25:29,080 --> 00:25:30,080
P'Three!

377
00:25:35,520 --> 00:25:38,640
You can go take photos
with them first, P'Three.

378
00:25:38,680 --> 00:25:39,560
I can wait.

379
00:25:40,400 --> 00:25:41,400
I don't want to.

380
00:25:42,680 --> 00:25:43,880
If anything, I'm already late.

381
00:25:43,920 --> 00:25:45,880
I should've just
carried you away sooner.

382
00:25:46,560 --> 00:25:49,360
Today is our first date.

383
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:51,800
I want to be your P'Three,

384
00:25:52,440 --> 00:25:54,000
not everyone else's Thr33Gamer.

385
00:25:56,800 --> 00:25:58,000
If things keep going like this,

386
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:00,200
I guess our date is over.

387
00:26:00,240 --> 00:26:00,920
Or...

388
00:26:01,360 --> 00:26:02,400
do you want to head back now?

389
00:26:03,480 --> 00:26:05,640
I'd like to stay
just a little bit longer.

390
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:08,680
I told you not to run.

391
00:26:08,920 --> 00:26:09,920
P'Three!

392
00:26:10,480 --> 00:26:11,680
P'Three!

393
00:26:12,080 --> 00:26:13,080
P'Three!

394
00:26:13,480 --> 00:26:14,280
They're leaving.

395
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:21,520
I know what we're gonna do now.

396
00:26:39,160 --> 00:26:41,440
(I got here first, so it's your treat.)

397
00:26:42,920 --> 00:26:45,920
(Yeah, fine. Order whatever you want.)

398
00:26:46,160 --> 00:26:48,320
(Get the paprika fried bananas for me.)

399
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:49,160
(I'm almost there.)

400
00:26:51,520 --> 00:26:53,760
There are people
who still eat something like this?

401
00:26:56,720 --> 00:27:00,240
I'll have the paprika fried bananas
and an iced Americano.

402
00:27:00,280 --> 00:27:01,720
Certainly. Please wait a moment.

403
00:27:11,160 --> 00:27:13,440
Our fates must be intertwined, huh?

404
00:27:14,400 --> 00:27:15,280
Met you again.

405
00:27:20,920 --> 00:27:22,080
I'm in a good mood.

406
00:27:22,600 --> 00:27:24,440
Could you please not ruin it?

407
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:26,560
I'd like to help,

408
00:27:27,160 --> 00:27:28,800
but I'm meeting someone here, too.

409
00:27:29,880 --> 00:27:33,200
Can I ruin your good mood
for a bit, then?

410
00:27:34,120 --> 00:27:34,880
Be my guest.

411
00:27:35,640 --> 00:27:36,840
But go sit at another table.

412
00:27:37,280 --> 00:27:38,520
Let's keep to ourselves.

413
00:27:45,640 --> 00:27:47,600
One iced latte, less sugar, please.

414
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:49,040
Certainly. Just a moment.

415
00:27:58,480 --> 00:28:00,240
(Which table are you at?)

416
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:04,400
(New message)

417
00:28:06,160 --> 00:28:08,600
(The first table.
You'll see me as soon as you walk in.)

418
00:28:09,920 --> 00:28:11,040
(New message)

419
00:28:17,280 --> 00:28:19,120
Here are your paprika fried bananas.

420
00:28:28,840 --> 00:28:29,760
It's you?

421
00:28:36,040 --> 00:28:36,920
Why?

422
00:28:37,560 --> 00:28:38,600
Are you disappointed

423
00:28:39,200 --> 00:28:41,080
that the friend
who's always listened to your problems

424
00:28:41,200 --> 00:28:43,720
and said goodnight
to you every night is me?

425
00:28:47,400 --> 00:28:48,400
Seriously,

426
00:28:49,240 --> 00:28:50,640
how much longer
are you going to mess with my head?

427
00:28:54,720 --> 00:28:57,680
Is it really that fun
to play with my feelings?

428
00:28:59,040 --> 00:29:00,360
Who said I was playing?

429
00:29:01,840 --> 00:29:03,720
So you're saying that all this time,

430
00:29:04,120 --> 00:29:05,600
you were actually being sincere with me?

431
00:29:08,120 --> 00:29:08,880
I don't know.

432
00:29:10,080 --> 00:29:11,400
Figure it out yourself.

433
00:29:12,320 --> 00:29:14,400
You're an expert
at jumping to conclusions anyway.

434
00:29:15,720 --> 00:29:17,120
What's the point of me saying anything?

435
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:40,200
P'Three, where did you go?

436
00:29:42,360 --> 00:29:43,800
Probably not him.

437
00:29:49,240 --> 00:29:51,200
He must have gone home already.

438
00:29:59,840 --> 00:30:01,200
That was a close call.

439
00:30:02,960 --> 00:30:04,120
What's this?

440
00:30:04,680 --> 00:30:05,800
A bear with a monkey face?

441
00:30:06,080 --> 00:30:08,040
And I'm a monkey with a bear face?

442
00:30:08,880 --> 00:30:09,600
Really?

443
00:30:11,560 --> 00:30:12,760
I'm sorry.

444
00:30:13,240 --> 00:30:16,240
I must have panicked
and mixed them up.

445
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:18,200
You're a derpy kid through and through.

446
00:30:18,280 --> 00:30:20,840
You can just be a bear, then.

447
00:30:21,040 --> 00:30:22,280
Hey, no way.

448
00:30:22,720 --> 00:30:25,520
I don't want to steal the spotlight
from the bear-head gamer.

449
00:30:31,160 --> 00:30:32,360
I'm sorry, Soh.

450
00:30:32,960 --> 00:30:35,240
The game of winning your heart
wasn't fun at all, was it?

451
00:30:36,120 --> 00:30:39,280
Nothing went as planned.

452
00:30:39,960 --> 00:30:43,200
In my head, I imagined
a super romantic date.

453
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:45,240
Look at how it turned out.

454
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:47,280
Taking you to eat snails,

455
00:30:47,880 --> 00:30:49,880
and when I finally brought you
where you wanted to come,

456
00:30:49,920 --> 00:30:52,160
we got interrupted again.

457
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:58,680
I wouldn't be surprised
if the game was over today.

458
00:31:01,680 --> 00:31:04,520
You asked me earlier

459
00:31:04,560 --> 00:31:06,360
what my type was.

460
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:10,800
Actually, I've never really had a type.

461
00:31:13,040 --> 00:31:14,720
But today, I've realized

462
00:31:15,360 --> 00:31:16,760
exactly what my type is.

463
00:31:21,320 --> 00:31:22,720
My type...

464
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:27,480
is someone who's hot-tempered and loud.

465
00:31:27,520 --> 00:31:28,440
(Are you even driving?)

466
00:31:28,480 --> 00:31:30,240
- But when he's serious,
- (Where are you going, the moon?)

467
00:31:30,240 --> 00:31:31,880
he's the most reliable person.

468
00:31:33,320 --> 00:31:34,960
He might seem a bit unfriendly

469
00:31:35,280 --> 00:31:36,640
and be a bit of a show-off.

470
00:31:36,880 --> 00:31:37,880
(It's my regular spot.)

471
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:39,720
(Usually, it's incredibly hard
to get a reservation here.)

472
00:31:39,880 --> 00:31:42,440
But he's actually very kind.

473
00:31:43,040 --> 00:31:44,920
He's down-to-earth
and not a picky eater at all.

474
00:31:47,960 --> 00:31:50,800
Even though he says
he doesn't like cute things,

475
00:31:51,320 --> 00:31:52,520
if it's something I like,

476
00:31:53,280 --> 00:31:54,680
he ends up humoring me anyway.

477
00:31:56,880 --> 00:31:58,520
Whenever I'm with him,

478
00:31:59,120 --> 00:32:02,400
I feel like I've become a kid again.

479
00:32:04,960 --> 00:32:06,960
- Oh, P'Three...
- Hey, P'Three!

480
00:32:27,440 --> 00:32:28,400
So,

481
00:32:29,640 --> 00:32:31,360
even if today didn't go as planned

482
00:32:31,400 --> 00:32:33,040
or wasn't as perfect as you expected,

483
00:32:33,520 --> 00:32:35,040
I just want to tell you that

484
00:32:35,600 --> 00:32:37,040
I'm very happy,

485
00:32:37,320 --> 00:32:38,720
and I had a lot of fun.

486
00:32:40,280 --> 00:32:43,280
Plus, I got to see another side of you,

487
00:32:44,200 --> 00:32:46,640
one that isn't just Thr33Gamer
or a big brother.

488
00:32:48,560 --> 00:32:49,200
I mean,

489
00:32:50,120 --> 00:32:53,880
are you just lying
to make me feel better?

490
00:32:56,680 --> 00:32:58,080
I don't lie. I keep the Five Precepts.

491
00:33:08,240 --> 00:33:11,880
Then let's...

492
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:13,640
go see Moo Deng, shall we?

493
00:33:14,440 --> 00:33:16,400
Sure. I want to see her.

494
00:33:16,720 --> 00:33:19,200
Well, before we go see Moo Deng,
the bouncy hippo,

495
00:33:19,800 --> 00:33:21,360
can I...

496
00:33:24,480 --> 00:33:25,800
see your bouncy hips first?

497
00:33:25,920 --> 00:33:27,240
Come on, what are you talking about?

498
00:33:27,280 --> 00:33:28,640
Hey, why?

499
00:33:29,400 --> 00:33:30,200
I won't let you.

500
00:33:30,200 --> 00:33:32,960
Hey, your cheeks
are bouncy and squishy, too.

501
00:33:43,800 --> 00:33:47,280
I guess I don't have to ask
if you had a good time today.

502
00:33:48,320 --> 00:33:49,920
I'm just so happy

503
00:33:50,640 --> 00:33:53,640
that you're no longer running away
from my feelings for you.

504
00:33:58,160 --> 00:34:00,840
And now, when my birthday comes around,

505
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:03,400
what gift could possibly top
how I feel today?

506
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,160
How is that my fault?

507
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:06,680
By the way,

508
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:08,760
when is your birthday?

509
00:34:08,880 --> 00:34:10,560
Christmas Day. Cool, right?

510
00:34:11,120 --> 00:34:12,200
- Really?
- Yeah.

511
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:13,640
Then it's coming up pretty soon.

512
00:34:14,560 --> 00:34:18,840
Is there anything you want as a gift?

513
00:34:19,360 --> 00:34:21,040
Nothing too expensive, please.

514
00:34:21,240 --> 00:34:22,760
I need to save up first.

515
00:34:25,240 --> 00:34:27,000
There's actually something I want,

516
00:34:27,520 --> 00:34:28,520
and it's not expensive.

517
00:34:29,400 --> 00:34:30,960
I definitely won't rob you.

518
00:34:32,000 --> 00:34:33,280
It's something that

519
00:34:34,120 --> 00:34:35,280
you can give me.

520
00:34:39,320 --> 00:34:41,480
But if you don't tell me,

521
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:43,280
I'll never know.

522
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:47,160
Come to my room, then you'll find out.

523
00:34:50,720 --> 00:34:52,480
I'm heading off, then.

524
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:46,960
(BS.THR33 wants to be your Lover.
I'll protect you.)

525
00:36:14,160 --> 00:36:14,840
Hey.

526
00:36:17,400 --> 00:36:19,360
You came all the way to my place
just to give me sh*t?

527
00:36:20,520 --> 00:36:22,080
Are you obsessed
with getting sh*t from me or what?

528
00:36:24,880 --> 00:36:26,280
Then why did you come here?

529
00:36:27,360 --> 00:36:28,760
To make me pay for the bananas?

530
00:36:37,680 --> 00:36:38,960
My mom told me to give this back to you.

531
00:36:47,600 --> 00:36:48,560
I'm leaving.

532
00:36:48,640 --> 00:36:49,720
Wait, Jack.

533
00:36:54,280 --> 00:36:55,280
I just realized something.

534
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:57,000
Tomorrow is Sunday.

535
00:36:58,680 --> 00:36:59,880
Wanna come up for a few drinks?

536
00:37:22,160 --> 00:37:23,080
This room of yours

537
00:37:23,800 --> 00:37:24,960
never changes, does it?

538
00:37:25,800 --> 00:37:26,680
Nothing but booze.

539
00:37:27,000 --> 00:37:28,080
Still no water.

540
00:37:29,720 --> 00:37:30,880
Why bother drinking water?

541
00:37:31,160 --> 00:37:32,000
It's pointless.

542
00:37:33,960 --> 00:37:34,840
And what about you?

543
00:37:35,280 --> 00:37:37,840
What made you agree
to drink with me tonight?

544
00:37:39,680 --> 00:37:41,320
I thought you'd hate me

545
00:37:42,440 --> 00:37:44,320
to the point of wanting me dead.

546
00:37:47,000 --> 00:37:47,880
To me,

547
00:37:48,920 --> 00:37:50,000
you're already dead.

548
00:38:02,920 --> 00:38:05,560
One shot, and you're done.

549
00:38:06,920 --> 00:38:09,200
I've killed you
thousands of times in the game,

550
00:38:10,520 --> 00:38:11,480
but in the end,

551
00:38:13,400 --> 00:38:15,080
I resurrect you every single time.

552
00:38:31,880 --> 00:38:32,880
You know what?

553
00:38:33,760 --> 00:38:34,880
I can't die,

554
00:38:35,680 --> 00:38:37,560
at least not in your memories.

555
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:43,720
And you know what else?

556
00:38:45,280 --> 00:38:47,280
If we finish this all at once,

557
00:38:48,800 --> 00:38:50,800
we won't remember a thing until morning.

558
00:38:52,120 --> 00:38:53,040
Why's that?

559
00:38:54,360 --> 00:38:55,880
What happens when morning comes?

560
00:38:57,760 --> 00:39:00,000
You and I might just go back
to hating each other

561
00:39:01,920 --> 00:39:03,280
and forget all about today.

562
00:39:06,800 --> 00:39:07,960
Just wait and see

563
00:39:08,360 --> 00:39:09,360
what happens tomorrow morning

564
00:39:09,640 --> 00:39:12,440
- between you and me.
- Then stay with me until then.

565
00:39:14,880 --> 00:39:15,680
Fine.

566
00:39:16,240 --> 00:39:17,360
I will.

567
00:39:41,560 --> 00:39:43,640
(Hey, happy...)

568
00:39:44,800 --> 00:39:46,520
(Christmas!)

569
00:39:53,600 --> 00:39:56,440
(Soh, guess what day it is.)

570
00:39:58,600 --> 00:39:59,800
It's...

571
00:39:59,800 --> 00:40:00,720
Christmas Day.

572
00:40:02,720 --> 00:40:04,320
Soh, today is my birthday.

573
00:40:04,360 --> 00:40:06,480
I'm actually getting mad.

574
00:40:08,240 --> 00:40:09,440
I know it's your birthday.

575
00:40:09,600 --> 00:40:11,080
I was just messing with you.

576
00:40:11,280 --> 00:40:12,920
(You're so nice,)

577
00:40:13,040 --> 00:40:14,600
(not like those B.S. Brothers guys.)

578
00:40:14,960 --> 00:40:17,000
They never remember my birthday.

579
00:40:20,040 --> 00:40:21,680
(Since it's my birthday today,)

580
00:40:22,080 --> 00:40:23,320
shall we go celebrate?

581
00:40:25,640 --> 00:40:26,840
I'm sorry, P'Three.

582
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:29,000
Actually, I'm busy...

583
00:40:29,720 --> 00:40:31,280
I have...

584
00:40:33,120 --> 00:40:34,640
a final project to finish.

585
00:40:37,200 --> 00:40:39,280
Come on, it's a special day.

586
00:40:39,320 --> 00:40:41,520
Are we really not going to
celebrate it together?

587
00:40:41,560 --> 00:40:43,680
Please? Stay with me, please.

588
00:40:44,640 --> 00:40:45,560
Or...

589
00:40:45,720 --> 00:40:46,800
should I come to you?

590
00:40:47,000 --> 00:40:47,880
No, you can't!

591
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:51,320
You can't.

592
00:40:51,800 --> 00:40:54,160
I have to go...

593
00:40:55,040 --> 00:40:56,360
shopping.

594
00:40:56,600 --> 00:40:57,600
Yeah.

595
00:40:57,880 --> 00:40:58,960
Yeah, shopping.

596
00:40:59,000 --> 00:41:00,280
(Shopping?)

597
00:41:00,400 --> 00:41:01,440
I thought you were doing a project.

598
00:41:03,080 --> 00:41:05,360
I'm buying stuff for the final project.

599
00:41:07,520 --> 00:41:11,360
Call me when you're free, then.
I'll be waiting.

600
00:41:11,440 --> 00:41:13,960
As for the birthday gift I asked for,

601
00:41:14,000 --> 00:41:15,520
no rush. Take your time.

602
00:41:15,520 --> 00:41:17,160
It's okay if it's a bit late.

603
00:41:17,160 --> 00:41:18,680
Even 15 minutes late is fine.

604
00:41:19,720 --> 00:41:20,440
Okay.

605
00:41:20,640 --> 00:41:22,960
I'll go buy the gift... Wait, no.

606
00:41:23,800 --> 00:41:27,000
I'll go buy things for the project now,

607
00:41:27,440 --> 00:41:28,120
okay?

608
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:29,720
Okay.

609
00:41:34,520 --> 00:41:35,720
Soh,

610
00:41:36,120 --> 00:41:38,760
was the last time you lied
back in second grade?

611
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:40,920
Am I going to get caught?

612
00:41:41,200 --> 00:41:42,200
What should I do?

613
00:41:42,640 --> 00:41:43,640
He won't suspect a thing.

614
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:47,040
He thinks you're purely derpy.

615
00:41:47,400 --> 00:41:48,760
He'd never think
you'd play him like that.

616
00:41:50,960 --> 00:41:52,600
That almost sounds like an insult.

617
00:41:57,400 --> 00:41:58,920
Do you guys have any idea

618
00:41:59,040 --> 00:42:02,400
what P'Three wants?

619
00:42:05,840 --> 00:42:06,640
You, obviously.

620
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:13,920
We should finish this quickly,

621
00:42:13,960 --> 00:42:15,640
so we can go shopping.

622
00:42:15,720 --> 00:42:17,000
If we're any later,

623
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:18,160
he's going to be really upset.

624
00:42:18,360 --> 00:42:19,440
Let's eat.

625
00:42:20,040 --> 00:42:22,320
Do you know what he wants, though?

626
00:42:23,400 --> 00:42:24,640
How should I know?

627
00:42:25,040 --> 00:42:26,160
You should've asked this guy.

628
00:42:26,600 --> 00:42:28,800
You've been with him lately.
What does he like?

629
00:42:30,160 --> 00:42:31,480
I don't know.

630
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:33,920
If I knew,
I wouldn't be asking you guys.

631
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:37,040
How would I know?

632
00:42:49,160 --> 00:42:50,160
Okay.

633
00:42:52,320 --> 00:42:53,600
You have the key?

634
00:42:53,720 --> 00:42:54,280
Yeah.

635
00:42:54,640 --> 00:42:56,880
It's not the first time
I've been to his place.

636
00:42:57,880 --> 00:42:58,840
Let's go.

637
00:43:05,080 --> 00:43:06,640
Happy Birthday, P'Three!

638
00:43:07,520 --> 00:43:10,000
Hey, P'Three! Merry Christmas...

639
00:43:11,440 --> 00:43:12,240
Soh...

640
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:45,920
♪Happy birthday to you♪

641
00:43:48,960 --> 00:43:52,920
♪Happy birthday to you♪

642
00:43:54,120 --> 00:44:00,160
♪Happy birthday, happy birthday♪

643
00:44:03,960 --> 00:44:09,800
♪Happy birthday to you♪

644
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:15,160
- Soh, I...
- Blow out the candles first.

645
00:44:30,040 --> 00:44:32,200
This salmon is amazing.

646
00:44:32,720 --> 00:44:35,120
We already ate some before we came here,

647
00:44:35,200 --> 00:44:36,680
so I'm pretty stuffed.

648
00:44:37,280 --> 00:44:38,720
It feels like I'm going to burst.

649
00:44:41,320 --> 00:44:42,280
- Soh...
- P'Three...

650
00:44:46,360 --> 00:44:50,080
I hope all your wishes come true.

651
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:04,760
- P'Jack, P'Laem.
- Yeah?

652
00:45:04,920 --> 00:45:08,400
I have to head back
and work on my project.

653
00:45:09,720 --> 00:45:11,520
I'll take my leave now.

654
00:45:13,520 --> 00:45:14,880
Wait, Soh!

655
00:45:28,240 --> 00:45:29,120
Soh!

656
00:45:29,640 --> 00:45:30,680
Soh!

657
00:45:31,280 --> 00:45:32,160
Soh!

658
00:45:33,600 --> 00:45:34,520
Soh!

659
00:45:36,360 --> 00:45:37,160
Soh...

660
00:45:58,080 --> 00:46:01,080
(Why do people
keep going back to their exes?)

661
00:46:20,240 --> 00:46:21,720
(What is it, P'Three?)

662
00:46:21,960 --> 00:46:23,880
Soh, can you open the door?

663
00:46:25,160 --> 00:46:27,000
(If you don't open the door,)

664
00:46:27,000 --> 00:46:28,680
(how am I supposed
to explain it to you?)

665
00:46:31,000 --> 00:46:31,800
I...

666
00:46:33,640 --> 00:46:34,920
I'm about to go to sleep.

667
00:46:35,200 --> 00:46:37,120
(I thought you said you don't lie.)

668
00:46:37,400 --> 00:46:38,920
The lights are still on.

669
00:46:42,320 --> 00:46:44,280
(I know you're not going to sleep yet.)

670
00:46:46,000 --> 00:46:48,040
How could you possibly know
better than I do?

671
00:46:51,480 --> 00:46:53,200
Can I have just five minutes?

672
00:46:53,360 --> 00:46:54,520
Just let me explain.

673
00:46:54,640 --> 00:46:56,360
If after you've heard me out,

674
00:46:57,000 --> 00:46:58,240
you want me to leave,

675
00:46:59,760 --> 00:47:00,800
I'll leave.

676
00:47:28,160 --> 00:47:29,480
Just five minutes.

677
00:47:44,960 --> 00:47:46,240
I told you,

678
00:47:46,880 --> 00:47:48,240
in my eyes,

679
00:47:49,040 --> 00:47:50,480
you're the only one.

680
00:47:55,520 --> 00:47:57,480
And right now,

681
00:47:58,040 --> 00:48:00,320
Belle and I are just friends.

682
00:48:01,440 --> 00:48:03,080
What happened between us
ended a long time ago.

683
00:48:09,440 --> 00:48:12,440
She came to see me today

684
00:48:13,440 --> 00:48:15,160
because she's going to study abroad.

685
00:48:15,240 --> 00:48:16,440
She just came to say goodbye

686
00:48:17,320 --> 00:48:19,680
and wish me a happy birthday.

687
00:48:23,760 --> 00:48:25,000
Before you arrived,

688
00:48:25,440 --> 00:48:27,880
she was bragging about her new guy,

689
00:48:28,280 --> 00:48:29,880
talking about
how great he is and all that.

690
00:48:30,920 --> 00:48:32,240
He's probably better than me.

691
00:48:32,840 --> 00:48:33,960
She wouldn't stop praising him.

692
00:48:34,640 --> 00:48:35,800
Are you jealous?

693
00:48:37,680 --> 00:48:38,960
It's not exactly jealousy.

694
00:48:39,040 --> 00:48:41,000
I just don't like
being compared to anyone.

695
00:48:42,920 --> 00:48:44,480
Try to imagine

696
00:48:44,640 --> 00:48:46,680
if I like someone else one day...

697
00:48:46,720 --> 00:48:48,240
Can you just not like someone else?

698
00:48:54,920 --> 00:48:57,360
I don't even want to think about
you liking someone else.

699
00:49:01,720 --> 00:49:02,440
How...

700
00:49:03,480 --> 00:49:05,040
How could I like someone else

701
00:49:06,000 --> 00:49:07,360
when the person I like

702
00:49:08,440 --> 00:49:09,800
is standing right here in front of me?

703
00:49:25,880 --> 00:49:28,160
I still want to play that game with you.

704
00:49:31,240 --> 00:49:34,320
The game you asked me
to play that night.

705
00:49:35,560 --> 00:49:37,840
The one where the start button...

706
00:49:40,920 --> 00:49:42,200
is right here.

707
00:49:56,200 --> 00:49:57,200
But for this game,

708
00:49:59,400 --> 00:50:00,960
I'm the only person
you're allowed to play with.

709
00:51:31,760 --> 00:51:32,880
(In a relationship)

710
00:51:32,920 --> 00:51:35,920
(Relationship established.)
(Lovers Lv.15)

711
00:51:49,760 --> 00:51:53,200
♪The answer is you
whenever I ask my heart,♪

712
00:51:53,200 --> 00:51:56,520
♪Can't get over you
though I try so hard♪

713
00:51:56,680 --> 00:52:00,520
♪I'm afraid that
love could pull us apart♪

714
00:52:00,560 --> 00:52:03,560
♪If I'm the only one
who's loving with all my heart♪

715
00:52:03,720 --> 00:52:06,840
♪So many times I've rehearsed the line♪

716
00:52:06,960 --> 00:52:10,360
♪To tell you that I wish you were mine,♪

717
00:52:10,400 --> 00:52:17,240
♪But I turn into a coward
every time you look in my eyes♪

718
00:52:17,440 --> 00:52:21,280
♪Maybe the risk is too high to take,♪

719
00:52:21,320 --> 00:52:24,760
♪Just being near you
is enough for my sake,♪

720
00:52:24,800 --> 00:52:31,560
♪But my heart beats so fast
that I can't fake♪

721
00:52:31,600 --> 00:52:34,760
♪I'll find my way
into your heart one day,♪

722
00:52:34,800 --> 00:52:37,400
♪Getting a little closer every day,♪

723
00:52:37,440 --> 00:52:40,000
♪Before you even look my way,♪

724
00:52:41,880 --> 00:52:44,840
♪Before you realize I'm here to stay♪

725
00:52:45,320 --> 00:52:48,440
♪For now,
I'll just keep things brotherly♪

726
00:52:48,480 --> 00:52:50,880
♪While caring for you secretly♪

727
00:52:50,920 --> 00:52:53,920
♪I'll leave no signs for you to see♪

728
00:52:55,160 --> 00:53:00,960
♪Until your heart makes room for me♪
